{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:18:21Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 15, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Keep my tasks when the server restarts\n2\t\n3\tSource: `docs/spec.md` (Taiga #5), as of the \"Decisions made here\" and\n4\t\"Acceptance criteria\" sections.\n5\t\n6\t## No design surface \u2014 this stage is a no-op\n7\t\n8\tEvery acceptance criterion in `docs/spec.md` is satisfied entirely inside\n9\t`backend/app/store.py`'s persistence logic and `backend/app/main.py`'s\n10\texisting routes, which are explicitly unchanged (spec's \"Affected areas\":\n11\t*\"`backend/app/main.py` \u2014 no changes expected. Every route already goes\n12\tthrough `store`; persistence is invisible to the route layer.\"*).\n13\t\n14\tChecking against what this role covers:\n15\t\n16\t- **API surface** \u2014 every route's request/response shape is unchanged\n17\t  (spec non-goals: *\"No change to `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 the `Task`\n18\t  shape on the wire is unchanged\"*). Nothing for a client to render\n19\t  differently.\n20\t- **Frontend** \u2014 spec's \"Affected areas\" states plainly: *\"Not affected:\n21\t  `frontend/` (entire directory)\"*. There is no new screen, component,\n22\t  state, loading/error/empty case, or interaction to spec \u2014 the existing\n23\t  frontend already just calls `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tasks*` and\n24\t  renders whatever comes back, and continues to do exactly that.\n25\t- **User-visible behavior change** \u2014 none, by design. The entire point of\n26\t  the feature (AC3, AC5, AC6) is that a restart is transparent: the app\n27\t  looks and behaves identically before and after this change, whether the\n28\t  data file is present, missing, or corrupt. There is no new state for a\n29\t  user to encounter \u2014 \"start empty on corrupt/missing data\" is not a new\n30\t  empty state UX, it's the *existing* empty-state UX (new task list, no\n31\t  tasks yet), reached via a different trigger.\n32\t\n33\tThere is accordingly no wireframe, component tree change, styling\n34\tdecision, or accessibility note to produce \u2014 introducing any would be\n35\tinventing UI the story's own non-goals rule out (*\"No new HTTP endpoint...\n36\tNo frontend change\"*).\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance criteria traceability\n39\t\n40\t| AC | Why no design element applies |\n41\t|----|-------------------------------|\n42\t| 1\u20132 | Write-on-mutation happens inside `TaskStore` methods, called from existing routes with no response shape change |\n43\t| 3\u20134 | Load-on-construct happens before the app serves any request; `GET /api/tasks` response shape is unchanged, so the existing frontend list rendering already handles it with no modification |\n44\t| 5\u20136 | \"Start empty\" is the app's current first-run/no-tasks appearance already \u2014 no new empty state to design |\n45\t| 7 | Directory creation is filesystem-internal, no observable surface |\n46\t| 8 | Test hermeticity is a backend test-infra concern, not a design concern |\n47\t\n48\t## Handoff\n49\t\n50\tStraight to **developer** \u2014 implement `docs/spec.md` as written, no\n51\t`docs/design.md` decisions to consume beyond this note confirming there\n52\tare none.\n53\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01G7ZVyvzGCDJnPtgsJt89Hy", "session_id": "fe73be77-94e3-47ae-8c3c-b0b404957ede"}}
